---
import SiteLayout from '../../components/SiteLayout.astro';
import '../../styles/site.css';
import '../../styles/mining-profitability.css';
---
<SiteLayout title="Monero Mining Profitability Calculator — Ember" description="Estimate expected XMR rewards, pool-adjusted revenue, electricity cost and operating balance from your own hashrate and manual network and price assumptions.">
  <div class="wrap mining-page">
    <header class="page-intro mining-intro">
      <span class="page-kicker">TOOLS / MINING ECONOMICS</span>
      <h1>Monero Mining Profitability Calculator</h1>
      <p>Build a transparent scenario from your own mining, network, reward and market assumptions. All numeric inputs start blank. This tool uses no live data and does not forecast future earnings.</p>
      <p class="manual-note">Manual assumptions · Calculated in this browser · Nothing is uploaded or saved</p>
    </header>

    <div class="mining-layout">
      <form id="mining-calculator" class="mining-form" novalidate>
        <div class="mining-section-head"><span class="eyebrow">01 / MINING SETUP</span><span class="section-hint">Your measured or benchmarked values</span></div>
        <div class="mining-fields">
          <div class="mining-field"><label for="miner-hashrate">Miner hashrate</label><span class="mining-input"><input id="miner-hashrate" name="minerHashrate" type="text" inputmode="decimal" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="hash-help hash-error"><span>H/s</span></span><small id="hash-help">Sustained hashrate while mining; rates vary with workload and test duration. Maximum 1,000,000,000 H/s.</small><span class="field-error" id="hash-error" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></span></div>
          <div class="mining-field"><label for="wall-power-watts">Whole-system wall power</label><span class="mining-input"><input id="wall-power-watts" name="wallPowerWatts" type="text" inputmode="decimal" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="power-help power-error"><span>W</span></span><small id="power-help">Measure the complete computer at the wall. Maximum 20,000 W.</small><span class="field-error" id="power-error" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></span></div>
          <div class="mining-field"><label for="mining-hours-per-day">Mining runtime</label><span class="mining-input"><input id="mining-hours-per-day" name="hoursPerDay" type="text" inputmode="decimal" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="hours-help hours-error"><span>hours / day</span></span><small id="hours-help">Active mining hours each day, from 0 to 24.</small><span class="field-error" id="hours-error" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></span></div>
          <div class="mining-field"><label for="electricity-price">Electricity tariff</label><span class="mining-input"><input id="electricity-price" name="electricityPricePerKwh" type="text" inputmode="decimal" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="tariff-help tariff-error"><span class="unit-currency" data-unit-currency>GBP / kWh</span></span><small id="tariff-help">Your rate per kWh in the selected currency. Standing charges and time-of-use variation are excluded; maximum 1,000 per kWh.</small><span class="field-error" id="tariff-error" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></span></div>
          <div class="mining-field"><label for="pool-fee-percent">Pool fee</label><span class="mining-input"><input id="pool-fee-percent" name="poolFeePercent" type="text" inputmode="decimal" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="fee-help fee-error"><span>%</span></span><small id="fee-help">Applied to estimated gross rewards; 0–100%.</small><span class="field-error" id="fee-error" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></span></div>
        </div>

        <div class="mining-section-head network-head"><span class="eyebrow">02 / NETWORK & REWARD</span><span class="section-hint">Use one network measure</span></div>
        <fieldset class="network-choice">
          <legend>Network basis</legend>
          <label><input type="radio" name="networkBasis" value="difficulty" checked> Network difficulty <span>hashes / block</span></label>
          <label><input type="radio" name="networkBasis" value="hashrate"> Network hashrate <span>H/s</span></label>
        </fieldset>
        <div class="mining-fields network-fields">
          <div class="mining-field" id="difficulty-wrap"><label for="network-difficulty">Network difficulty</label><span class="mining-input"><input id="network-difficulty" name="networkDifficulty" type="text" inputmode="decimal" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="difficulty-help difficulty-error"><span>hashes / block</span></span><small id="difficulty-help">Expected work to find one block. Must be greater than zero; maximum 1,000,000,000,000,000,000 hashes/block.</small><span class="field-error" id="difficulty-error" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></span></div>
          <div class="mining-field" id="network-hashrate-wrap" hidden><label for="network-hashrate">Network hashrate</label><span class="mining-input"><input id="network-hashrate" name="networkHashrate" type="text" inputmode="decimal" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="network-hash-help network-hash-error"><span>H/s</span></span><small id="network-hash-help">Estimated total network work per second. Must be greater than zero; maximum 10,000,000,000,000,000 H/s.</small><span class="field-error" id="network-hash-error" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></span></div>
          <div class="mining-field"><label for="expected-reward-per-block">Expected total block reward</label><span class="mining-input"><input id="expected-reward-per-block" name="expectedRewardPerBlock" type="text" inputmode="decimal" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="reward-help reward-error"><span>XMR / block</span></span><small id="reward-help">Enter an assumption for emission plus transaction fees, before pool fee. No reward is retrieved live; maximum 10 XMR/block.</small><span class="field-error" id="reward-error" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></span></div>
          <div class="mining-field"><label for="xmr-price">XMR price</label><span class="mining-input"><input id="xmr-price" name="xmrPrice" type="text" inputmode="decimal" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="price-help price-error"><span class="unit-currency" data-unit-currency>GBP / XMR</span></span><small id="price-help">Manual price in the selected currency. No market price or FX conversion is used; maximum 10,000,000 per XMR.</small><span class="field-error" id="price-error" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></span></div>
          <div class="mining-field"><label for="mining-currency">Display currency</label><select id="mining-currency" name="currency" aria-describedby="currency-help currency-status"><option value="GBP">GBP — £</option><option value="USD">USD — $</option><option value="EUR">EUR — €</option></select><small id="currency-help">Changing currency keeps your numbers but does not convert them. Enter the tariff and XMR price in the selected currency.</small><span class="currency-status" id="currency-status" aria-live="polite">Enter fiat assumptions in GBP.</span></div>
        </div>
        <button class="mining-reset" type="reset">Clear all assumptions</button>
      </form>

      <section class="mining-results" aria-labelledby="mining-results-title">
        <div class="mining-section-head"><span class="eyebrow">03 / ESTIMATED SCENARIO</span><span class="manual-tag">USER-SUPPLIED INPUTS</span></div>
        <h2 id="mining-results-title">Estimated net operating result</h2>
        <p class="result-context">Expected-value estimate under constant assumptions. Results are not guaranteed income or a prediction.</p>
        <p class="result-value" id="daily-net">Enter all assumptions to calculate</p>
        <p class="result-sign" id="result-meaning">Includes pool-adjusted expected revenue less electricity cost.</p>
        <div class="projection-wrap">
          <table class="projection-table">
            <caption>Constant-assumption projections</caption>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Estimate</th><th scope="col">Daily</th><th scope="col">30 days</th><th scope="col">365 days</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><th scope="row">Expected block equivalents</th><td data-period="1" data-key="expectedBlocks">—</td><td data-period="30" data-key="expectedBlocks">—</td><td data-period="365" data-key="expectedBlocks">—</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Expected XMR after fee</th><td data-period="1" data-key="netXmr">—</td><td data-period="30" data-key="netXmr">—</td><td data-period="365" data-key="netXmr">—</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Gross estimated revenue</th><td data-period="1" data-key="grossRevenue">—</td><td data-period="30" data-key="grossRevenue">—</td><td data-period="365" data-key="grossRevenue">—</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Pool fee value</th><td data-period="1" data-key="poolFeeValue">—</td><td data-period="30" data-key="poolFeeValue">—</td><td data-period="365" data-key="poolFeeValue">—</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Revenue after pool fees</th><td data-period="1" data-key="revenueAfterPoolFees">—</td><td data-period="30" data-key="revenueAfterPoolFees">—</td><td data-period="365" data-key="revenueAfterPoolFees">—</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Electricity consumption</th><td data-period="1" data-key="energyKwh">—</td><td data-period="30" data-key="energyKwh">—</td><td data-period="365" data-key="energyKwh">—</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Electricity cost</th><td data-period="1" data-key="electricityCost">—</td><td data-period="30" data-key="electricityCost">—</td><td data-period="365" data-key="electricityCost">—</td></tr>
              <tr class="net-row"><th scope="row">Estimated net</th><td data-period="1" data-key="estimatedNet">—</td><td data-period="30" data-key="estimatedNet">—</td><td data-period="365" data-key="estimatedNet">—</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="break-even">Break-even electricity tariff <strong id="break-even">—</strong> <span id="break-even-note">Available when electricity consumption is above zero.</span></p>
        <p class="mining-status" id="mining-status" aria-live="polite">Fill every numeric field to see a locally calculated estimate.</p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <section class="mining-explainer" aria-label="Calculator method and limitations">
      <figure class="mining-formula-flow" aria-labelledby="formula-flow-title" aria-describedby="formula-flow-caption">
        <span class="eyebrow">THE CALCULATION PATH</span>
        <h2 id="formula-flow-title">From work and assumptions to an operating estimate</h2>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Miner hashrate × runtime</strong><span>expected hashes</span></li>
          <li><strong>Expected hashes ÷ network difficulty</strong><span>expected block equivalents</span></li>
          <li><strong>Block equivalents × reward</strong><span>expected gross XMR</span></li>
          <li><strong>Gross revenue − pool fee</strong><span>revenue after pool fees</span></li>
          <li><strong>Revenue − electricity cost</strong><span>estimated net operating result</span></li>
        </ol>
        <figcaption id="formula-flow-caption">When network hashrate is selected instead, expected block equivalents are expected hashes ÷ (network hashrate × the 120-second target interval). All values are scenario inputs; this page fetches no live data.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <article><span class="eyebrow">METHOD / 01</span><h2>How the estimate is calculated</h2><p>Miner hashes equal hashrate × active seconds. Expected block equivalents are miner hashes ÷ difficulty, or miner hashes ÷ (network hashrate × 120 seconds). Difficulty and hashrate are different units; the target block interval connects them.</p><p>Expected XMR is expected block equivalents × your entered total block reward. The pool fee is subtracted from estimated rewards. Electricity is whole-system watts ÷ 1,000 × hours/day × days, then multiplied by your tariff.</p><p class="method-line"><code>Estimated net = revenue after pool fees − electricity cost</code></p><p>Daily, fixed 30-day and fixed 365-day projections use the same assumptions. They do not model future changes in difficulty, hashrate, reward, price or runtime.</p></article>
      <article class="mining-input-guide"><span class="eyebrow">INPUTS / 02</span><h2>Where to get each input</h2><p>Use values for the same machine, workload and time period. Mark what you measured, what you looked up and when you looked it up. This calculator cannot detect your hardware or retrieve current network or market conditions.</p><p id="mining-table-help">On narrow screens, focus a table region and use arrow keys, or swipe to scroll horizontally.</p><div class="mining-input-table-wrap" role="region" aria-label="Mining calculator input sources" aria-describedby="mining-table-help" tabindex="0"><table class="mining-input-table"><caption>Inputs and suggested sources</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Input</th><th scope="col">How to obtain or estimate it</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Miner hashrate</th><td>Use a sustained XMRig RandomX hashrate for the intended configuration, not a brief startup number. A controlled XMRig benchmark can help compare settings; pool-side short-window estimates fluctuate. Record the XMRig version and test duration.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Whole-system wall power</th><td>Measure the complete computer at the wall while it runs the representative workload, using a suitable plug-in power meter. Do not substitute CPU package power for the computer's total draw.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Mining hours per day</th><td>Choose the number of hours you expect to mine on a typical day. This is a scenario assumption, not a detected schedule.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Electricity tariff</th><td>Use the relevant per-kWh rate from your electricity bill or supplier account, in the selected currency. If your plan varies by time, use a representative rate and note that simplification.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Pool fee</th><td>Check the selected pool's own current fee and payout terms. Enter the fee as a percentage; pool-specific deductions or rules may differ from this simple model.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">XMR price</th><td>Choose an external market source and timestamp for your own scenario, then enter the value in the selected currency. No market source is endorsed or queried by this tool.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Network difficulty or hashrate</th><td>Use a dated value from a source you trust, such as your own synchronized Monero node/RPC or a named network-statistics source. Difficulty is hashes per block; hashrate is hashes per second. This page retrieves neither.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Expected block reward</th><td>Use a dated network or node source for the total block reward assumption, including emission and transaction fees, before pool fee. Rewards can change; the calculator does not obtain this value.</td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div><p class="input-source-note"><strong>Value types:</strong> hashrate and wall power are best measured; runtime is your planned scenario; tariff, pool fee, XMR price, network measure and reward are externally sourced assumptions. Worked examples below are explicitly hypothetical. Keep source names and timestamps with your notes.</p><p class="source-note">Technical references checked 10 October 2026: <a href="https://xmrig.com/docs/miner/benchmark" rel="external noreferrer">XMRig's benchmark documentation</a> describes versioned RandomX benchmark runs; <a href="https://web.getmonero.org/resources/moneropedia/block.html" rel="external noreferrer">Monero's block reference</a> describes the two-minute average target used when converting network hashrate to expected block equivalents. The tool uses the existing local calculation model and does not retrieve either source live.</p></article>
      <article class="mining-example"><span class="eyebrow">WORKED EXAMPLE / HYPOTHETICAL</span><h2>Follow one invented daily scenario</h2><p class="synthetic-note"><strong>Teaching values only.</strong> These numbers are invented to demonstrate the implemented arithmetic. They are not current network, price, pool, hardware or earnings data and should not be used as a realistic mining estimate.</p><dl class="example-assumptions"><div><dt>Miner hashrate</dt><dd>1,000 H/s</dd></div><div><dt>Whole-system power</dt><dd>100 W</dd></div><div><dt>Runtime</dt><dd>24 hours/day</dd></div><div><dt>Tariff</dt><dd>£0.20/kWh</dd></div><div><dt>Pool fee</dt><dd>1%</dd></div><div><dt>XMR price</dt><dd>£150/XMR</dd></div><div><dt>Network difficulty</dt><dd>86,400,000,000 hashes/block</dd></div><div><dt>Total block reward</dt><dd>0.6 XMR</dd></div></dl><div class="mining-example-table-wrap" role="region" aria-label="Hypothetical daily calculation table" aria-describedby="mining-table-help" tabindex="0"><table class="mining-example-table"><caption>Daily calculation from those hypothetical inputs</caption><tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Active time and expected hashes</th><td>24 × 3,600 = 86,400 seconds; 1,000 × 86,400 = 86,400,000 hashes</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Expected block equivalents</th><td>86,400,000 ÷ 86,400,000,000 = 0.001</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Expected gross XMR</th><td>0.001 × 0.6 = 0.0006 XMR</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Pool fee and expected XMR after fee</th><td>0.0006 × 1% = 0.000006 XMR fee; 0.0006 − 0.000006 = 0.000594 XMR</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Revenue after pool fee</th><td>0.0006 × £150 = £0.09 gross; £0.09 × 1% = £0.0009 fee; £0.09 − £0.0009 = £0.0891</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Electricity</th><td>(100 ÷ 1,000) × 24 = 2.4 kWh; 2.4 × £0.20 = £0.48</td></tr>
        <tr class="example-result"><th scope="row">Estimated net operating result</th><td>£0.0891 − £0.48 = <strong>−£0.3909 per day</strong></td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div><p>The worked result includes only modeled pool-adjusted expected revenue minus electricity. It does not represent an individual payout or total business profitability. Pool payout methods and share luck vary; network difficulty and price can change; hardware cost, depreciation, cooling, maintenance, taxes and other costs are excluded. The live calculator uses the same math, but none of these example values are prefilled.</p></article>
      <article><span class="eyebrow">READ THE RESULT / 02</span><h2>Expected value is not a payout</h2><p>This is a simplified pool-style expected-value model. Fractional block equivalents describe a proportional average, not individual block discoveries. Pool payout methods, luck, thresholds, stale shares, downtime and fees can make realized payouts differ.</p><p>It is not a solo-mining probability simulator, P2Pool payout model or named pool estimate. It excludes hardware purchase and depreciation, taxes, cooling, internet, other operating costs, pool-specific rules and changes in energy prices.</p><p>The expected block reward is a user assumption: enter emission plus transaction fees before pool fee. Results describe a scenario, not investment guidance or an Ember desktop-app capability.</p></article>
      <article><span class="eyebrow">LIMITS / 03</span><h2>Keep the result in context</h2><p>Expected value is not a payout. Fractional block equivalents describe a proportional average, not individual block discoveries. Pool payouts vary with pool policy, share luck, thresholds, stale shares, downtime and fees. Difficulty and price can change; this calculator holds your assumptions constant across each horizon.</p><p>A positive operating estimate is not total business profitability. Hardware purchase and depreciation, cooling, maintenance, taxes, internet and other costs are excluded. This is not a solo-mining probability simulator, a P2Pool or named-pool payout model, investment guidance, or an Ember desktop-app capability.</p><p>All numeric values start blank. Calculations run locally in your browser; inputs are not uploaded or saved. Choosing GBP, USD or EUR changes display labels only and does not convert your entered tariff or XMR price.</p><p>For source context, read <a href="/learn/randomx-memory-cache/">RandomX memory and cache</a>, <a href="/learn/xmrig-cpu-threads/">XMRig CPU threads</a>, the <a href="/troubleshoot/xmrig-low-hashrate/">low-hashrate checklist</a>, and the <a href="/guides/xmrig-windows-setup/">Windows setup guide</a>. For electricity-only arithmetic, use the <a href="/tools/electricity-cost-calculator/">electricity cost calculator</a>.</p></article>
    </section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
<script>import '../../scripts/mining-profitability.js';</script>
